\cf2 A squad of Elvi burst into the studio, prised Rusty and Pacer apart and brought them to their feet, keeping their arms pinned so they couldn\'92t resume their tearing at each other.\
\'94We should use the lyrics the Great Teacher wrote for us,\'94 Pacer hurled as he struggled to break free.\
\'93What? They stink worse than week-old road-kill. The Great Teacher has lost his edge,\'94 Rusty shot back.\
Everyone in the studio and control room except Chanta sucked in their breaths and looked side-eye at him. Chanta closed his eyes and hoped everyone would fade away before he opened them again. He stifled a little yearning sigh. He missed Sarah, and he missed the little guy growing inside her, and couldn\'92t shake the solid belief his lyrical talents would return if only they were with him. They were his inspiration.\
\'93The Great Teacher\'92s words are still better than anything you could write,\'94 Pacer bristled. \'93Even your song titles: 
\f2\i Don\'92t Cry Daddy
\f1\i0 ? 
\f2\i Momma Liked the Roses
\f1\i0 ? What do you think you\'92re writing, some sad family soap opera?\'94\
\'93
\f2\i My
