\cf2 The day wore on. Chanta became more unnerved by the Elvi\'92s religious fervour to denounce religion, yet praise \'93the One\'94 as their prophetic guardian. Yet Chanta was also relieved; no one had pressured him to produce any lyrics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 As day became night, the tablets stayed out. The Elvi had moved on from religion to Dawkins\'92 science and were especially amused that all humans, Airborne 
\f2\i and
\f1\i0  Cloudborne, were descended from monkeys.\
\'93Same ancestors as us, the lot of them,\'94 one said, and all the others agreed.\
\'93Maybe the next leap comes from down here. From Cloudborne stock,\'94 another said, to much encouragement.\
\'93Or Elvi genes,\'94 said another, and the room went silent.\
Chanta\'92s sense of unease returned aflame when one Elvi started singing a tune, and all the others quickly joined. At first, Chanta heard the angelic harmonies more than words. As if rising from a trance, he became aware of the lyrics only as the song was reaching its end:\
\

\f2\i Evolve me tender,\
Evolve me true,\
The Dawkins dream fulfilled,\
For my Darwin I love you.\
And I always will.
\f1\i0 \
\
The Elvi erupted with a cheering roar, mobbed Chanta, and lifted him high above their heads. In a seething mass, they surged towards the living room door, perhaps to carry him exultantly out to the street. Unfortunately, they slammed him head-first into the beam above the door. He fell to the floor like a dropped cheeseburger\'97with extra sauce\'97apparently dead.\
Silently and reverently, a chosen few carried Chanta to his room and laid him gently on his unmade bed. Some kissed his forehead. Others hunkered down to keep vigil over his body.\
\
